  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 520.02 Approval Criteria for Forestry Projects",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 520.02 Approval Criteria for Forestry Projects. In addition to meeting the criteria established in Env-Wt 300, the department shall not approve a forestry project unless the following criteria are met:\n\n(a) The project is exclusively for the purpose of timber harvesting and forest management;\n\n(b) Skid trails and truck roads associated with the project are exclusively for the purpose of accessing viable tree stands and conducting forestry projects;\n\n(c) The project will be conducted in accordance with RSA 227-J, RSA 482-A, RSA 483, RSA 483-B, RSA 485-A, and RSA 212-A; and\n\n(d) The project will be conducted in accordance with the design and construction requirements specified in Env-Wt 520.04.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
